###
### Laravel DDD API Testing
###
### Instructions:
### 1. First run the "Register" request to create a user
### 2. Run the "Login" request and copy the token from the response
### 3. Replace all {{auth_token}} with your actual token, or set up environment variables
### 4. Make sure to use HTTPS (https://localhost) and ignore SSL warnings
###
### To set up environment variables in VS Code REST Client:
### Create a file named "http-client.env.json" in the root directory with:
### {
###   "dev": {
###     "auth_token": "your_token_here"
###   }
### }
###### Register
POST https://localhost/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "John Doe",
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "password_confirmation": "password123"
}

### Login (Copy token from response)
POST https://localhost/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Get Current User (me)
GET https://localhost/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer 19|Z3rN7p6EsaF7HhqwcODyTvnNqbIKGG1Dny4D09kT909e5628
Accept: application/json

### Logout
POST https://localhost/api/v1/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}
Accept: application/json

### Refresh Token
POST https://localhost/api/v1/auth/refresh
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}
Accept: application/json

### List Users
GET https://localhost/api/v1/users
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}
Accept: application/json

### Search Users
GET https://localhost/api/v1/users/search?q=john
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}
Accept: application/json

### Get User by ID
GET https://localhost/api/v1/users/3
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}
Accept: application/json

### Update User
PUT https://localhost/api/v1/users/3
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "John Updated"
}

### Delete User
DELETE https://localhost/api/v1/users/3
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}
Accept: application/json

###
### Alternative: Manual Token Usage
### If automatic token capture doesn't work, copy the token from login response
### and replace YOUR_TOKEN_HERE with the actual token
###

### Manual Login (copy token from response)
POST https://localhost/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Manual - Get Current User
GET https://localhost/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE
Accept: application/json
